Done. Two files changed:

**`rust/src/lib.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
Exact match on each note's `tags` vector, preserves input order.

**`rust/src/main.rs`** — wired `--tag <TAG>` into the `list` command:
- Imports `filter_by_tag` and `Note` from `notekeep`
- Scans args for `--tag`; if found, reads the next arg as the tag value and passes it through `filter_by_tag`
- Without the flag, behaves exactly as before (lists all notes)

Build: `cargo check` passes cleanly.


